Below is a **step‑by‑step guide** that takes you from the very first wireframe to a fully‑deployed, production‑ready e‑commerce front‑end.  
I’ll cover the whole stack (design → code → testing → deployment) and give you concrete examples, snippets, and best‑practice tips that you can copy‑paste into your own project.

---

## 1. Planning & Design

| What | Why | Tool |
|------|-----|------|
| **Define core user flows** (search → product page → cart → checkout) | Keeps the UI focused on real tasks | User story map |
| **Create wireframes** | Visualise layout before coding | Figma / Sketch / Adobe XD |
| **Design a component library** | Reusable UI elements (buttons, cards, modals) | Storybook |
| **Plan responsive breakpoints** | Mobile‑first design | CSS Grid / Flexbox |
| **Sketch accessibility** | WCAG compliance | axe DevTools |

> **Tip:** Keep a shared design system (colors, typography, spacing) in a single place (e.g., a `tokens.css` file or a design‑system repo).

---

## 2. Tech Stack Decision

| Category | Options | Recommendation |
|----------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React** (most community, ecosystem) |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, SCSS, Tailwind CSS, Styled‑Components | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first, fast prototyping) |
| **State** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, React Context | **Redux Toolkit** (predictable, devtools) |
| **Routing** | React Router | ✅ |
| **API Calls** | Axios, Fetch | **Axios** (built‑in interceptors) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library | ✅ |
| **Build** | Vite, Create‑React‑App, Next.js | **Vite** (fast dev, ES modules) |
| **Deployment** | Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (auto‑SSR, preview URLs) |

> **Why Vite?**  
> - Lightning‑fast dev server (HMR).  
> - Native ESM support → no bundling during dev.  
> - Easy to add plugins (e.g., Tailwind, ESLint).

---

## 3. Project Skeleton

```bash
ecommerce-frontend/
├─ public/
│  ├─ index.html
│  └─ favicon.ico
├─ src/
│  ├─ assets/
│  ├─ components/
│  │  ├─ ui/          # Buttons, inputs, modals
│  │  ├─ layout/      # Header, Footer, Sidebar
│  │  └─ pages/       # ProductList, ProductDetail, Cart, Checkout
│  ├─ store/          # Redux slices
│  ├─ hooks/          # Custom hooks (useCart, useAuth)
│  ├─ services/       # API clients
│  ├─ utils/          # helpers, formatters
│  ├─ App.jsx
│  └─ main.jsx
├─ .env
├─ .gitignore
├─ package.json
├─ tailwind.config.js
└─ vite.config.js
```

---

## 4. Core Components (React + Tailwind)

### 4.1 Product Card

```tsx
// src/components/ui/ProductCard.tsx
import { Link } from 'react-router-dom';
import { Product } from '../types';

export interface ProductCardProps {
  product: Product;
}

export const ProductCard: React.FC<ProductCardProps> = ({ product }) => (
  <div className="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
    <Link to={`/product/${product.id}`}>
      <img
        src={product.image}
        alt={product.title}
        className="w-full h-48 object-cover"
      />
      <div className="p-4">
        <h3 className="font-semibold text-lg truncate">{product.title}</h3>
        <p className="text-gray-600">${product.price.toFixed(2)}</p>
      </div>
    </Link>
  </div>
);
```

### 4.2 Cart Icon (Header)

```tsx
// src/components/layout/Header.tsx
import { useSelector } from 'react-redux';
import { RootState } from '../../store';
import { Link } from 'react-router-dom';

export const Header = () => {
  const cartCount = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.cart.items.length);

  return (
    <header className="flex justify-between items-center p-4 bg-white shadow">
      <Link to="/" className="text-2xl font-bold">Shop</Link>
      <Link to="/cart" className="relative">
        <svg className="w-6 h-6" ...>…</svg>
        {cartCount > 0 && (
          <span className="absolute -top-2 -right-2 bg-red-500 text-white rounded-full w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center text-xs">
            {cartCount}
          </span>
        )}
      </Link>
    </header>
  );
};
```

---

## 5. State Management (Redux Toolkit)

```ts
// src/store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import { Product } from '../types';

interface CartState {
  items: Product[];
}

const initialState: CartState = { items: [] };

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addToCart(state, action: PayloadAction<Product>) {
      state.items.push(action.payload);
    },
    removeFromCart(state, action: PayloadAction<number>) {
      state.items = state.items.filter(p => p.id !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart(state) {
      state.items = [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addToCart, removeFromCart, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

```ts
// src/store/index.ts
import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import cartReducer from './cartSlice';

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: { cart: cartReducer },
});

export type RootState = ReturnType<typeof store.getState>;
export type AppDispatch = typeof store.dispatch;
```

```tsx
// src/main.jsx
import { Provider } from 'react-redux';
import { store } from './store';
import App from './App';

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <Provider store={store}>
    <App />
  </Provider>
);
```

---

## 6. API Layer

```ts
// src/services/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL,
  timeout: 10000,
});

api.interceptors.request.use(config => {
  // Add auth token if available
  const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  return config;
});

export default api;
```

```ts
// src/services/products.ts
import api from './api';
import { Product } from '../types';

export const fetchProducts = async (): Promise<Product[]> =>
  (await api.get('/products')).data;

export const fetchProductById = async (id: number): Promise<Product> =>
  (await api.get(`/products/${id}`)).data;
```

---

## 7. Routing (React Router v6)

```tsx
// src/App.jsx
import { BrowserRouter as Router, Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom';
import { Header } from './components/layout/Header';
import { ProductList } from './components/pages/ProductList';
import { ProductDetail } from './components/pages/ProductDetail';
import { CartPage } from './components/pages/CartPage';
import { CheckoutPage } from './components/pages/CheckoutPage';

export default function App() {
  return (
    <Router>
      <Header />
      <main className="container mx-auto p-4">
        <Routes>
          <Route path="/" element={<ProductList />} />
          <Route path="/product/:id" element={<ProductDetail />} />
          <Route path="/cart" element={<CartPage />} />
          <Route path="/checkout" element={<CheckoutPage />} />
        </Routes>
      </main>
    </Router>
  );
}
```

---

## 8. Page Example – Product List

```tsx
// src/components/pages/ProductList.tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { fetchProducts } from '../../services/products';
import { ProductCard } from '../ui/ProductCard';
import { Product } from '../../types';

export const ProductList = () => {
  const [products, setProducts] = useState<Product[]>([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchProducts().then(setProducts).finally(() => setLoading(false));
  }, []);

  if (loading) return <p>Loading…</p>;

  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      {products.map(p => (
        <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

